From 6021dddc844fce40b8336a2e3196870b0038dfd8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kacper Paczos <kacperpaczos2024@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 00:40:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 07/14] pack(linux): ship web standalone runtime (fix packaged
 web sidecar boot)

Every Linux package (dir/AppImage/deb/rpm) quit with exit 75 because the
packaged web sidecar ran in server mode: resolveToolPackWebOutputMode
pinned linux to "server", so the sidecar loaded next.config.ts from the
packaged @open-design/web package and died on workspace-root file reads
(readFileSync(resolve(WORKSPACE_ROOT, file)) with no apps/web/ tree in a
packaged install). The mac/win lanes avoid this by materializing the
Next.js standalone tree into packaged resources; the Linux lane had no
equivalent.

- config: drop the linux "server" pin so linux resolves webOutputMode
  exactly like the desktop platforms (default standalone, OD_WEB_OUTPUT
  _MODE override honored); webOutputMode already participates in the
  workspace-build cache key, so the linux node rebuilds cleanly.
- linux lane: mirror the mac after-pack pipeline - writeWebStandalone
  HookConfig (same env contract, same assertWebStandaloneOutput error
  clarity), afterPack registration in the builder config, post-build
  assertLinuxWebStandaloneResource over linux-unpacked/resources, and
  webOutputMode in open-design-config.json so apps/packaged resolves
  webStandaloneRoot to <resourcesPath>/open-design-web-standalone and
  spawns the standalone server (no apps/packaged changes needed).
- resources/linux/web-standalone-after-pack.cjs: linux-owned hook (the
  shared mac/win hook's pruning/hyperframes/signing steps are platform-
  owned behavior this lane does not perform). Copies the traced tree
  verbatim, links the pnpm public-hoist area to the tree root (pnpm-
  shaped standalone trees otherwise let requires escape through the
  build machine's ancestor node_modules), prunes dangling symlinks, and
  fails the build when the closure is not self-contained.
- guard: allowlist the new linux hook cjs (same compatibility entry
  class as the shared hook).
